hello games no man sky is not full of  men but it is full of sky actually quite  a lot of sky I got a better look at it  recently and there's a couple new things  that we didn't know about before for  starters there are NPCs there aliens you  discover them and interact with them as  you travel across the universe in search  of the mysterious center you can learn  the aliens languages by using monoliths  scattered throughout the planets or  through trading and the more that you  understand them the better items they'll  be willing to barter with you for in  order to trade in the first place you'll  need resources which you can find on  planets or in space on fact no man sky  has its own periodic table and while it  does include elements like plutonium and  carbon which we have in our world  there's a whole bunch of new elements  that we will discover along the way you  scavenge resources to upgrade your stuff  in the environment so you can say shoot  a tree and collect carbon or shoot  crystals and collect plutonium or while  you're in your ship in space destroying  another ship will yield carbon these  elements can be used to upgrade your  suit your weapon and your ship your ship  is pretty self-explanatory  shields better lasers but your suit and  your weapon are a little more  complicated I can't show you this but I  was able to upgrade my weapon with a  small bomb these small bombs allowed me  to alter the terrain even allowing me to  discover underground caves and  underground ponds on one such planet I  discovered one of these caves and used  it as shelter since my suit was too weak  to protect me from the cold that's the  other thing you'll be upgrading your  suit on planets that are too cold or too  hot you have to upgrade your suit to  deal with the varying temperatures or to  say prevent you from breathing in a  toxic atmosphere your suit protects you  and your weapon defends you so you'll be  spending most of your resources on these  two things but that's it there's no  character levelling system there's no  progression no skill trees all of your  resources and all of your upgrading  energy will be focused on your stuff I  mentioned this before but it's true  you won't be running into anyone in no  man's sky nor will you be able to drop  your coordinates to another friend and  have them come and join you the  developers told me that the chances of  running into another player are super  slim like less than 1% because you  verse is so big and everyone will begin  the game on a different planet when they  boot up it doesn't sound like there's  any true multiplayer but they did  compare the ability to interact with  other players similar to how you do in  Dark Souls or journey which are two  totally separate things so it's still  very unclear and while there is no  overarching plot there is one thing that  hello Games Sean Murray says will be  what compels you to complete Nomad sky  and that's the desire to find the center  of the universe the developers are still  being vague about what it is that will  compel you to find the center of the  universe but according to Murray that  will be your overarching goal I had a  lot of fun exploring planets and finding  new creatures and of course naming them  silly things some of those creatures are  genuinely terrifying larger than life  brontosaurus like beings that absolutely  dwarfed me and some of them were  absolutely adorable but I did have some  trouble with the flying the controls  still feel really floaty they're not  really tight and gently nudging the  analog stick sent me flying in one  direction so I imagine flying will take  some getting used to  I did get a little motion sick which did  dampen my enjoyment of flying through  space but everything around me was so  beautiful it took my attention away from  that queasy feeling no man's sky still  looks amazing the colors are bright and  vivid and nothing quite beats running  through a field of red grass under a  clear lime-green sky so if you're  looking forward to no man's sky  pre-orders are open and you don't have  to wait long the game will be out on  June 21st for everything else you need  to know about no man's sky stay tuned to  game spot calm  you
 

